  "question": {
    "text": "A car is moving towards a high cliff. The driver sounds a horn of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>.&nbsp;The reflected sound heard by the driver has frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is the velocity of sound, then the velocity of the car, in the same velocity units, will be",
    "image": null
  },
